## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of retrieval basics: chunking, embeddings, and vector stores in a compact, beginner‑friendly setup.

## Key Concepts
- Chunking strategy, embedding model choice, cosine similarity
- In-memory vector store for low latency
- Simple re-ranking using exact-term hits
- Latency and memory considerations in small-scale apps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal pseudo-code: chunk, embed, store, search
async function chunk(text, size=400){ /* split into chunks */ }
async function embed(text){ /* call embedding API */ }
async function search(query, chunks){
  const q = await embed(query);
  const sims = chunks.map(c => ({ chunk: c, score: cosine(q, c.vec) }));
  sims.sort((a,b) => b.score - a.score);
  // simple re-ranking by term matches
  return sims.slice(0,3).sort((a,b)=>hitScore(b.chunk, query) - hitScore(a.chunk, query));
}
```

