## Why This Is Asked

Demonstrates a concrete, beginner-friendly plan to evaluate how tokenization choices influence attention in a multilingual setting, including preserving domain terms and generating actionable metrics.

## Key Concepts

- Tiny Transformer architectures and tokenization workflows
- Attention maps and per-token signaling across languages
- Tokenization strategies: BPE vs unigram and their impact on domain terms
- Evaluation metrics and masking rules for brand terms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-runner to compute per-prompt attention-signal
function attentionSignal(attentions, sentimentIndices) {
  // attentions: [layers][heads][from][to], sentimentIndices: array
  let total = 0, count = 0;
  for (const layer of attentions) {
    for (const head of layer) {
      for (const idx of sentimentIndices) {
        for (const j of head) {
          total += j[idx];
          count++;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return count ? total / count : 0;
}
```

